Cheap things.

An item has a name (text) and a price (money).

The cheap names in some items (a list of items) under a limit (money) is a list of texts:
its name in upper case for each item in the items whose price is less than the limit.

Suppose tea is an item with name "tea" and price 2.5.
Suppose cake is an item with name "cake" and price 4.0.
For example, the cheap names in a list of tea and cake under 3 joined with "," is "TEA".
For example, the cheap names in a list of tea and cake under 1 joined with "," is "".
